From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:59:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] scripts: Add ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 as a known device

The ROG Xbox Ally X20's AMS740LS02 OLED has no display profile, so
gamescope only exposes the two EDID modes and the frame limiter has no
refresh rates between 60 and 120 Hz. The EDID declares a 30-120 Hz
native range and builds its own 60 Hz mode by stretching the vertical
front porch at the 120 Hz pixel clock.

Add VFP timings for 30-120 Hz rounded to the nearest line from the
120 Hz base mode, and give it content-driven HDR like we did for the
Legion Go 2.
